<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>MailDigest — package repositories</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body { max-width: 46rem; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1.2rem;
         font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif; }
  h1 { margin-bottom: .2rem; }
  p.sub { margin-top: 0; opacity: .75; }
  pre { padding: .9rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; border-radius: 6px;
        background: rgba(127,127,127,.14); }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; }
  footer { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: .9rem; opacity: .7; }
</style>

<h1>MailDigest</h1>
<p class="sub">Version @VERSION@ — package repositories for apt and dnf.
<a href="https://github.com/kpafi/maildigest">Source on GitHub</a></p>

<h2>Debian, Ubuntu, Kali (apt)</h2>
<p>Add the key and the repository once:</p>
<pre><code>curl -fsSL https://kpafi.github.io/maildigest/apt/maildigest-archive-keyring.gpg \
  | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/maildigest-archive-keyring.gpg &gt; /dev/null

echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/maildigest-archive-keyring.gpg] \
https://kpafi.github.io/maildigest/apt stable main" \
  | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/maildigest.list

sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt install maildigest</code></pre>
<p>From then on <code>apt upgrade</code> carries new versions along on its own.
Supported are Debian 13 and newer, Kali Rolling and Ubuntu 24.04 and newer.</p>

<h2>Fedora (dnf)</h2>
<pre><code>sudo dnf copr enable kpafi/maildigest
sudo dnf install maildigest</code></pre>

<h2>Without a package repository</h2>
<pre><code>pipx install git+https://github.com/kpafi/maildigest</code></pre>

<footer>The packages are signed with the repository key; apt verifies the
signature on every fetch. The key is bound to this one repository via
<code>signed-by</code> and is trusted for nothing else on the system.</footer>
</html>
